          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 13.3: Let us find out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.192,
            0.743,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": "z Take some parts of plants like stem cutting of a money plant, the ‘eyes’ of a sprouted potato, or a piece of ginger (Fig. 13.11b)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.23,
            0.744,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": "z Plant each of them separately in moist soil (not too deep). For money plant, you can just put a cutting in a glass container which makes it easy to observe."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.783,
            0.179,
            0.89,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": "",
